{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '225,267p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py; sed -n '95,154p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py; jq '{target_selection,scientific_validity}' task/resources/final/protocol.json; sed -n '1,45p' .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md; cat results/conclusions.md\"","aggregated_output":"        if np.all(accumulated >= deficits):\n            break\n    for column in selected[::-1]:\n        trial = [item for item in selected if item != column]\n        if wins(trial):\n            selected = trial\n    if len(selected) <= 1 or time.monotonic() >= deadline:\n        return _answer(selected)\n    maximum_deficit = int(deficits.max())\n    relevant = deficits > maximum_deficit - 2 * len(selected)\n    reduced = coefficients[relevant]\n    requirements = deficits[relevant]\n    available = np.flatnonzero(gains > 0)\n    reduced = reduced[:, available]\n    ranked = np.sort(reduced, axis=1)[:, ::-1]\n    cumulative = np.cumsum(ranked, axis=1)\n    lower_bound = int(np.max(np.sum(cumulative < requirements[:, None], axis=1) + 1))\n    if lower_bound >= len(selected):\n        return _answer(selected)\n    for budget in range(lower_bound, len(selected)):\n        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:\n            break\n        search_order = np.argsort(-gains[available], kind='stable')\n        try:\n            found = _borda_search(reduced, requirements, budget, search_order, deadline)\n        except TimeoutError:\n            break\n        if found is not None:\n            trial = available[found].tolist()\n            if wins(trial):\n                selected = trial\n                break\n    return _answer(selected)\n\n\ndef _solve(matrix, target, rule, fraction, tolerance, deadline, context):\n    original = matrix[target]\n    caps = np.round(original + fraction * (1 - original), 10)\n    if rule == 'borda':\n        return _borda_solve(matrix, target, caps, tolerance, deadline, context)\n    return _scalar_solve(matrix, target, rule, caps, tolerance, context)\n\n\n    endpoints = np.unique(np.concatenate((original, caps)))\n    best = None\n    for lower in endpoints:\n        upper_candidates = endpoints[\n            (endpoints >= lower)\n            & ((endpoints + lower) / 2 - competitor >= -tolerance)\n        ]\n        if not len(upper_candidates):\n            continue\n        upper = upper_candidates[0]\n        low_needed = max(0, half + 1 - np.count_nonzero(original >= lower))\n        high_needed = max(0, half - np.count_nonzero(original >= upper))\n        shared = np.flatnonzero((original < lower) & (caps >= upper))\n        low_only = np.flatnonzero(\n            (original < lower) & (caps >= lower) & (caps < upper)\n        )\n        high_only = np.flatnonzero(\n            (original >= lower) & (original < upper) & (caps >= upper)\n        )\n        if low_needed > len(shared) + len(low_only):\n            continue\n        if high_needed > len(shared) + len(high_only):\n            continue\n        shared_count = min(len(shared), max(low_needed, high_needed))\n        selected = shared[:shared_count].tolist()\n        selected += low_only[:max(0, low_needed - shared_count)].tolist()\n        selected += high_only[:max(0, high_needed - shared_count)].tolist()\n        if best is not None and len(selected) >= len(best):\n            continue\n        if wins(selected):\n            best = selected\n    return best\n\n\ndef _scalar_solve(matrix, target, rule, caps, tolerance, context):\n    original = matrix[target]\n    aggregate = np.mean if rule == 'mean' else np.median\n    rival_scores = context[rule]\n    competitor = max(rival_scores[:target].max(initial=-np.inf),\n                     rival_scores[target + 1:].max(initial=-np.inf))\n\n    def wins(indices):\n        attacked = original.copy()\n        attacked[indices] = caps[indices]\n        return float(aggregate(attacked) - competitor) >= -tolerance\n\n    if wins([]):\n        return {'status': 'feasible', 'tasks': []}\n    if not wins(list(range(len(original)))):\n        return {'status': 'unattainable', 'tasks': []}\n    if rule == 'mean':\n        selected = _mean_budget(original, caps, wins)\n    elif len(original) % 2:\n        selected = _odd_median_budget(original, caps, competitor, tolerance)\n    else:\n        selected = _even_median_budget(original, caps, competitor, tolerance, wins)\n    if len(original) <= 6:\n        reference = _exhaustive(original, caps, wins)\n        if selected is None or reference is None or len(selected) != len(reference):\n            selected = reference\n{\n  \"target_selection\": \"Rank-stratified nonwinners under the original arithmetic mean; stable content-hash row order; linearly spaced positions including best nonwinner and worst. Freeze full eligible population before search. Smoke first 12 rows and one target only.\",\n  \"scientific_validity\": \"Independent input integrity, rank/witness/bound checks, real code execution, matched nonvacuous controls and replay. No candidate flags certify learning, exactness or validity. No adaptivity or learning-state gate: this is static discrete optimization.\"\n}\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\n_No conclusions yet._\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
